# macOS Contribution Context

- Upstream CDUMM development is primarily Windows-based.
- This fork contributes macOS implementation and gameplay validation.
- Some Windows-only ASI behaviors are adapted as native macOS runtime modules.
- Keep platform-specific behavior isolated and preserve existing Windows paths.
- Before committing or pushing runtime-mod behavior, obtain gameplay
  validation of the exact candidate from the contributor.
- Keep an English iteration record for every change that states why it was
  needed, what changed, what it resolved, and the current test result.
- Submit every CDUMM-related online message, including issues, pull requests,
  reviews, and comments, to the contributor for explicit approval before
  publishing it.

# Public Contribution Hygiene

- Write all newly added or modified repository content in English.
- Never commit personal information, usernames, or machine-specific paths.
- Use repository-relative paths in code and documentation.
- Never commit store account data, local library paths, launch configuration,
  manifests, identifiers, or runtime state.
- Never commit API keys, tokens, cookies, sessions, or credentials.
- Never commit game executables, resources, extracted assets, binary fragments,
  or hashes of commercial binaries.
- Do not copy third-party mod source or payloads without compatible licensing.
- Keep reverse-engineered addresses, UUIDs, and instruction signatures in
  local untracked configuration.
- Keep generated libraries, archives, compatibility manifests, and runtime
  receipts untracked.
- Inspect the complete diff for non-English text and sensitive data before
  committing or publishing.
